---
title: Treacle Tart
source: https://www.daringgourmet.com/treacle-tart/
servings: 8
cook time: 40 minutes
prep time: 25 minutes
total time: 1 hour 35 minutes
---

For the shortcrust pastry, place @all-purpose flour{1.75%cups} and @salt{1/2%tsp} in a #food processor{} and pulse to blend. Add cold @unsalted butter{5%Tbsp} and cold @vegetable shortening{5%Tbsp} (or additional cold unsalted butter) and pulse a few times until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs. Add @ice water{1/3%cup} a little at a time, pulsing between additions, until the dough holds together when pressed between your fingers without over-mixing.

Form the dough into a ball, flatten into a 1-inch thick disk, wrap in plastic wrap, and refrigerate for at least ~{30%minutes}.

Preheat the #oven{} to 375°F. Roll out the chilled pastry dough with a #rolling pin{} until slightly larger than a #9-inch tart pan{} with a removable bottom. Fit the pastry into the tart pan, trim the excess, and prick the bottom multiple times with a #fork{}.

Line the pastry crust with parchment paper, fill with dried beans or pie weights, and bake on the middle shelf for 10 to ~{15%minutes}. Remove the beans and parchment paper and bake for another 5 to ~{10%minutes}, until the crust is a very pale golden.

While the crust blind-bakes, prepare the filling. Place @golden syrup{1.25%cups}, @lemon zest{1%lemon}, and @lemon juice{1%Tbsp} in a medium #saucepan{} over low heat until hot and runny. Stir in @fresh white breadcrumbs{1.25%cups}, turn off the heat, and let sit for ~{5%minutes}.

In a small #bowl{}, lightly beat @egg{1} and @heavy cream{3%Tbsp} together with a fork. Pour the egg mixture into the warm syrup mixture and stir quickly to combine.

Pour the filling into the par-baked tart crust and bake at 375°F on the middle shelf for 20 to ~{25%minutes}, until the pastry is golden and the filling is set and nicely browned. Let cool before slicing and serving warm with clotted cream, whipped cream, custard, or ice cream.

Tip: Substituting vegetable shortening (or all butter) for traditional lard keeps the pastry lacto-ovo vegetarian while staying flaky.
